# Documentation

Project docs live in `docs/`, organized by [Diataxis](https://diataxis.fr/):

- `docs/tutorials/` — learning, end to end
- `docs/how-to/` — task recipes
- `docs/reference/` — facts, mirror the code
- `docs/explanation/` — rationale and direction
- `docs/index.md` — the map of all docs (start here)

Docs are the source of truth for architecture, workflows, and conventions; skills and rules point into them.

## Finding the right doc

Each doc has YAML front-matter with `related_code`, `related_docs`, and `keywords`. To find docs about a file, search `docs/` for that path in `related_code`. Start from `docs/index.md`.

## Keeping docs current (required)

When a change touches code, update docs in the same change:

- Update every doc whose `related_code` lists a file you changed; set its `last_reviewed` to today.
- New/removed source file, target, or directory → update `reference/source-layout.md`.
- New behavior/workflow → update the matching how-to or reference; if a new doc is added, also add it to `docs/index.md`.
- Keep facts (C++20, presets, targets, paths) consistent with `CMakeLists.txt`, `src/CMakeLists.txt`, `CMakePresets.json`.

For a full sweep after larger changes, use the `update-docs` skill.
